From 0e259659f09b47c79c04ac9157af284cc70a1604 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: davidcanar <davidcanar@localhost>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:58:16 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] TP cross-host: read back recurrent wshift from the
 non-output rank worker

A cross-host non-output rank runs every pass on a real child worker whose
pickled copy of the exported recurrent states is where the DSV4/SWA ring
shift (wshift) is written; restore_tp_params() only saw the driver-side
exports, so the shift was dropped, window_beg never advanced, and ring
addressing went stale once position outgrew the ring (~750 tokens on
DS4.1: window 128 + 2*256 slack = 768 ring rows). mp_model_forward now
returns the walk wshifts as the pass result on those ranks, and
forward_tp/prefill_tp fetch that tiny result synchronously and copy it
onto the driver exports before restore_tp_params(), so post_advance()
advances window_beg exactly like on the output rank. Output-rank,
single-host, warmup and single-module paths unchanged (tests/tp).
---
